Description:
Noise-C is a plain C implementation of the Noise Protocol Framework. Chromium
vendors it here as a standalone third-party target for future browser-side
localhost policy and transport integrations that require Noise handshakes.

Local Modifications:
None to upstream sources.

Chromium integration files added:
- BUILD.gn
- DIR_METADATA
- OWNERS
- README.chromium

Build-specific behavior:
- The Chromium GN target currently builds the reference protocol, protobuf, and
  key-loading libraries.
- Curve25519, Ed25519, ChaChaPoly, AES-GCM, SHA-256, SHA-512, BLAKE2b, and
  BLAKE2s are enabled.
- Curve448 and NewHope are not wired into the Chromium target yet.
